13. ABSTRACT(_mum 2OOwords)
A series of electrically heated robe experiments was performed to investigate the effect of high aspect ratio on cmvatme heat transfer enhancement in uniformly heated rectangular cooling passages. Three hardware geometries were tested; a baseline straight aspect ratio 10 robe, an aspect ratio 1 (square) robe with a 45 ° curve, and an aspect ratio 10 tube with a 45 ° curve. Gaseous nilrogen with the following properties was used as the coolant: ambient inlet temperature, pressures to 8.3 MI_ wall-to-bulk temperature ratios less than two, and Reynolds numbers based on hydraulic diameter ranging from 250,000 to 1,600,000. The measured curvature enhancement factors were compared to values predicted by three previously published models which had been developed for low aspect ratio robes. The models were shown to be valid for the high aspect ratio tube as well the low aspect ratio robe, indicating that aspect ratio had tittle impact on the curvaua'e heat transfer enhancement in these tests.
